# class Holder { get lone() { return this.inner.lone } get inner() {} }  unknown = hand(new Holder())  for (..) unknown.inner
# What a getter reads under its own name does not say that anything else enters the getter: nothing else reads under `lone`, and the host enters it once.
# The read under `lone` in its body, and the read of the loop, may enter `inner`
# FORM: AsRead
# RUN: heat-graph flow
# RUN(CLASSES): heat-graph flow classes

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
layout L0 kind=Instance name="Holder" constructor=f1

function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="hand" [isFreeName]
    v2 = NewClosure function=f1
    v3 = NewClass v2 layout=L0
    v4 = NewClosure function=f2
    DefineMethod v3, v4 layout=L0 methodKind=Getter key="lone"
    v6 = NewClosure function=f3
    DefineMethod v3, v6 layout=L0 methodKind=Getter index=1 key="inner"
    v8 = FinishClass v3 layout=L0
    v9 = Construct v8
    v10 = Call v1, -, v9
    v11 = ToBoolean v1
    Jump -> next b1()
  b1():
    LoopHint
    v13 = PropGet v10 key="inner"
    Branch v11 -> taken b2(), notTaken b3()
  b2():
    Jump -> next b1()
  b3():
    Return
}
function f1 name="Holder" kind=BaseConstructor flags=[HasNewTarget] results=[{type=anything}] {
    v1 = GetConstructPrototype v0 layout=L0
    v2 = NewObject v1 layout=L0
    Return v2
}
function f2 name="lone" kind=Getter flags=[HasThis] thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything):
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="inner"
    v2 = PropGet v1 key="lone"
    Return v2
}
function f3 name="inner" kind=Getter flags=[HasThis] thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
    Return
}
# CHECK: f2 size 3 mass 3.000000: f3*1.000000
# CHECK-NOT: *
# CHECK: host: f0*1.000000 f2*1.000000 f3*1.000000
# CLASSES: f2 size 3: f3*1.000000
# CLASSES-NOT: *
# CLASSES: host: f0*1.000000 f2*1.000000 f3*10.000000
# CLASSES-NEXT: unknown:
# CLASSES-NEXT: activations:
